---
/**
 * The corrections, collected.
 *
 * Every guide on this site ends up correcting something — a threshold that is
 * not in the law, a requirement no lender actually publishes, a rule imported
 * from somewhere else. Those corrections are the most useful paragraphs here
 * and they are also the hardest to find, because each one sits in the middle of
 * the guide it belongs to.
 *
 * This page is only a collection. Nothing is asserted here that a guide has not
 * already asserted and sourced, and an entry whose guide has not published yet
 * is left out rather than linked to a 404 — so the page fills itself in as the
 * schedule runs.
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { MYTHS } from '../data/myths';
import { getCategory } from '../lib/categories';
import { livePosts } from '../lib/livePaths';

const bySlug = await livePosts();

// An entry is only shown once the guide behind it is live. That keeps the one
// rule this page has: every correction here has been published and sourced
// somewhere you can go and check.
const entries = MYTHS.flatMap((m) => {
  const post = bySlug.get(m.guide);
  if (!post) return [];
  return [{ ...m, post, category: getCategory(post.data.category) }];
});

const waiting = MYTHS.length - entries.length;

// Grouped so the page reads as a map of the subject rather than a list.
const order = ['banking', 'loans', 'cars', 'business', 'cost-of-living', 'employment'];
const groups = order
  .map((slug) => ({
    meta: getCategory(slug),
    items: entries.filter((e) => e.category.slug === slug),
  }))
  .filter((g) => g.items.length > 0);
---

<Layout
  title="Money in Korea: What Everyone Gets Wrong"
  description="The thresholds, limits and requirements foreigners in Korea are told about that are not in any law — each one corrected against the statute or the lender's own published terms."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
    <header class="mb-10 border-b border-rule pb-8">
      <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-[0.7rem] tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-soft/60 uppercase">
        Reference · corrections from across the guides
      </p>
      <h1 class="mb-4 font-display text-[2.5rem] leading-tight font-bold text-ink sm:text-[2.9rem]">
        What everyone gets wrong
      </h1>
      <p class="max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft/85">
        Most bad advice about money in Korea is not a lie. It is a real rule from
        one bank, one office or one year, repeated until it sounds like the law.
        These are the ones that come up most, and what the statute or the
        lender’s own published terms actually say.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-3 font-mono text-[0.78rem] text-ink-soft/70">
        <span><strong class="text-ink">{entries.length}</strong> corrections</span>
        <span><strong class="text-ink">{groups.length}</strong> subjects</span>
        {
          waiting > 0 && (
            <span>
              <strong class="text-ink">{waiting}</strong> waiting on a scheduled guide
            </span>
          )
        }
      </div>
    </header>

    {
      groups.map((group) => (
        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="mb-5 flex items-baseline gap-3 border-b border-rule pb-2">
            <span class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink">
              {group.meta.shortTitle}
            </span>
            <a
              href={`/${group.meta.slug}/`}
              class="font-sans text-[0.8rem] font-medium text-ink-soft/60 underline decoration-rule underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:text-gold hover:decoration-gold"
            >
              All {group.meta.shortTitle.toLowerCase()} guides
            </a>
          </h2>

          <ol class="space-y-8">
            {group.items.map((e) => (
              <li>
                <p class="mb-2 flex items-start gap-2.5">
                  <span
                    class="mt-[0.3rem] flex-none font-mono text-[0.8rem] font-bold text-ink-soft/40"
                    aria-hidden="true"
                  >
                    ✕
                  </span>
                  <span class="font-display text-[1.15rem] leading-snug font-semibold text-ink-soft/70 line-through decoration-ink-soft/30">
                    {e.claim}
                  </span>
                </p>
                <p class="mb-3 max-w-2xl pl-[1.6rem] text-[1rem] leading-relaxed text-ink">
                  {e.reality}
                </p>
                <p class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1 pl-[1.6rem] font-sans text-[0.8rem]">
                  <span class="text-ink-soft/60">{e.basis}</span>
                  <span class="text-ink-soft/30" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                  <a
                    href={e.guide}
                    class="font-medium text-ink underline decoration-gold/50 decoration-2 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-gold"
                  >
                    {e.post.data.title}
                  </a>
                </p>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </section>
      ))
    }

    <section class="border-t border-rule pt-6">
      <h2 class="mb-3 font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">
        How something gets onto this page
      </h2>
      <p class="max-w-2xl text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft/85">
        Only by being corrected in a guide first, against a statute, a
        regulator, or a lender’s own published product terms — never against
        another article. Each line above is a summary; the guide beside it
        carries the citation and the reasoning, and logs it if the rule later
        moves. Where a correction is “there is no such rule”, that is a
        statement about what the law contains, not a promise about how the
        counter in front of you will behave: a bank may still apply its own
        internal policy, and it is allowed to.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl font-sans text-[0.85rem] text-ink-soft/65">
        If something here has gone out of date, or a rule you were quoted is not
        on this page, <a
          href="/contact/"
          class="text-ink-soft/85 underline decoration-slate-300 underline-offset-2 hover:text-gold">tell us</a
        > — that is how most of these were found.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
